## Part 1 — Azure Portal: RBAC Configuration

### Step 1 — Create a Security Group

A Microsoft Entra ID security group was created to centralise permission management and support group-based access control.

### Step 2 — Add a User to the Group

The lab user was added to the security group, allowing membership to be managed centrally.

### Step 3 — Assign RBAC Permissions

The following configuration was applied:

| Setting           | Configuration  |
| ----------------- | -------------- |
| Scope             | Resource group |
| Role              | Reader         |
| Assignment target | Security group |

The Reader role provides visibility into resources within the assigned scope without granting permission to modify them.

### Result

The group-based role assignment was configured at resource group scope. The effective access of individual users depends on the applicable role assignment, group membership, and scope.

