## Security Considerations

* Use least-privilege permissions when accessing Azure resources and Microsoft Graph.
* Verify the active tenant and subscription before performing administrative operations.
* Review group membership and role assignments regularly.
* Treat guest accounts as identities that require appropriate access review.
* Avoid publishing personal email addresses, tenant identifiers, subscription identifiers, user object IDs, access tokens, or other sensitive environment details in public repositories.
* Interpret empty API results carefully; validate permissions and query scope before drawing conclusions.

---

## Key Learning Points

* Azure CLI can validate the active Azure account context.
* Microsoft Graph supports programmatic investigation of tenant users and devices.
* Member and guest identities can be examined through directory data.
* Azure RBAC, directory identity management, and device registration are distinct areas of the Azure security architecture.
* API-based investigation complements portal-based administration.
* Clear documentation should distinguish observed results from assumptions about their causes.

